  "cues": [
   [
    0.106,
    "In the nineteen seventies, scientists warned that certain industrial chemicals could damage the ozone layer."
   ],
   [
    6.742,
    "In nineteen eighty-five, they found proof: a region of severely thinned ozone above Antarctica, and it came back every year, larger and deeper."
   ],
   [
    17.048,
    "To measure ozone, scientists use Dobson units."
   ],
   [
    20.705,
    "Imagine squeezing all the ozone above one spot down to the ground: one Dobson unit is a layer just one hundredth of a millimetre thick."
   ],
   [
    30.186,
    "Before nineteen seventy-nine, Antarctic readings never fell below two hundred and twenty Dobson units."
   ],
   [
    36.888,
    "So any area below that line is called the ozone hole."
   ]
  ]
 },
