    0.106,
    "Why over the poles?"
   ],
   [
    1.516,
    "In the polar winter, strong winds circle the pole, a polar vortex, and lock the cold air in."
   ],
   [
    8.245,
    "It gets so cold that thin clouds form in the stratosphere, polar stratospheric clouds."
   ],
   [
    14.016,
    "On their icy surfaces, chlorine and bromine from industrial chemicals are turned into very reactive forms."
   ],
   [
    21.529,
    "When the Sun returns in late winter and early spring, they attack the ozone all at once, and the hole opens."
   ],
   [
    28.83,
    "The Antarctic hole is the largest, but the Arctic has had serious losses too, notably in two thousand eleven and two thousand twenty."
   ]
